# Changelog & Agent Long-Term Memory

The `changelog/` directory is the **persistent memory** for Cursor agents on this project. All non-trivial work must be recorded here before and during implementation.

## Folder layout

```text
changelog/
└── {DATESLUG}/              # YYYY-MM-DD (work date)
    └── {LAYERNAME}/         # primary architectural layer
        ├── INVESTIGATION{N}.md
        ├── IMPLEMENTATION{N}.md
        ├── CODE_REVIEW{N}.md
        ├── PERFORMANCE_AUDIT{N}.md   # optional; often under performance/ folder
        ├── CODE_HEALTH_AUDIT{N}.md   # optional; often under code-health/ folder
        └── REFACTOR{N}.md            # optional; often under refactor/ folder
```

**Example:** `changelog/2026-07-21/domain/INVESTIGATION1.md`

## Naming conventions

| Token | Format | Values |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `{DATESLUG}` | `YYYY-MM-DD` | ISO date of the work session |
| `{LAYERNAME}` | lowercase | `domain`, `application`, `interface`, `infrastructure`, `entrypoint`, `performance`, `code-health`, `refactor`, `tests` |
| `{N}` | integer, no zero-pad | `1`, `2`, `3` … monotonic **per layer folder** |
| File prefix | UPPERCASE | `INVESTIGATION`, `IMPLEMENTATION`, `CODE_REVIEW`, `PERFORMANCE_AUDIT`, `CODE_HEALTH_AUDIT`, `REFACTOR` |

**Pairing rule:** `IMPLEMENTATION{N}.md` must reference and implement the matching `INVESTIGATION{N}.md` in the same folder.

**Review rule:** `CODE_REVIEW{N}.md` should reference the matching `INVESTIGATION{N}.md` and `IMPLEMENTATION{N}.md` when reviewing that increment. `{N}` is monotonic per layer folder, same as investigation/implementation numbering.

**Multi-layer work:** use one folder per layer (e.g. `changelog/2026-07-21/domain/` and `changelog/2026-07-21/infrastructure/`).

## Agent memory protocol

### Before starting work

1. Scan `changelog/**/` for existing `INVESTIGATION*.md`, `IMPLEMENTATION*.md`, `CODE_REVIEW*.md`, `PERFORMANCE_AUDIT*.md`, `CODE_HEALTH_AUDIT*.md`, and `REFACTOR*.md` related to the request (same layer, feature, or date).
2. Read open items: `Status: draft`, `planned`, or `in_progress`.
3. Prefer continuing an existing pair over creating duplicates.
4. When creating new files, list the folder and pick the next `{N}` — never overwrite without explicit user approval.

### During work

- **Investigate first** → write `INVESTIGATION{N}.md` (gap analysis, minimal increment, scope in/out).
- **Plan second** → write `IMPLEMENTATION{N}.md` with an ordered checklist.
- **Execute third** → check off tasks (`- [x]`), update `Status` fields.
- Note deviations from the investigation inside the implementation file.

### After completing work

- Set `IMPLEMENTATION{N}.md` → `Status: done`; set investigation → `approved` when accurate.
- Summarize outcomes in the implementation file if scope changed.
- Deferrals go in investigation **Scope (out)** — do not lose them in chat.

### What agents must not do

- Skip changelog files for feature, refactor, or scaffold work.
- Store decisions only in chat (chat is ephemeral; `changelog/` is memory).
- Commit secrets or `.env` content in changelog files.

## File roles

| File | Purpose | Written when |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `INVESTIGATION{N}.md` | Architecture alignment, gaps, minimal increment | Before code |
| `IMPLEMENTATION{N}.md` | Checklist, task order, completion criteria | Before code; updated during execution |
| `CODE_REVIEW{N}.md` | Branch/code review vs changelog plans and architecture | After implementation; before merge |
| `PERFORMANCE_AUDIT{N}.md` | Evidence-based bottleneck findings vs `reference.md` rubric | Performance audit; before hardening or when latency is a concern |
| `CODE_HEALTH_AUDIT{N}.md` | Dead/duplicate/redundant/AI-smell findings vs `reference.md` rubric | Code health audit; before refactors or cleanup sprints |
| `REFACTOR{N}.md` | Merged change/remove/wire/consolidate actions from performance + code-health audits | Refactor planning (refactor-planner agent); before cleanup implementation |

Canonical templates: investigation/implementation workflow in `.cursor/agents/incremental-layer-builder.md`; code review workflow in `.cursor/agents/changelog-code-reviewer.md`; performance audit workflow in `.cursor/agents/performance-auditor.md` (rubric: `.cursor/agents/performance-auditor/reference.md`); code health audit workflow in `.cursor/agents/code-health-auditor.md` (rubric: `.cursor/agents/code-health-auditor/reference.md`); refactor synthesis workflow in `.cursor/agents/refactor-planner.md`. Architecture constraints: `ARCHITECTURE.md`. Environment commands: `ENVIRONMENT_SETUP.md`.

## Task ordering in IMPLEMENTATION checklists

`domain` → `application` → `infrastructure` → `interface` → `entrypoint` → tests → `uv run ruff` → `uv run mypy` → `uv run pytest`

## Status values

| File | Allowed `Status` |
| :--- | :--- |
| INVESTIGATION | `draft`, `approved` |
| IMPLEMENTATION | `planned`, `in_progress`, `done` |
| CODE_REVIEW | `draft`, `final` |
| PERFORMANCE_AUDIT | `draft`, `final` |
| CODE_HEALTH_AUDIT | `draft`, `final` |
| REFACTOR | `draft`, `final` |
